  "summary": "Messages queue cleared under RBC-RX-05: 7 items across 3 patients, all closed. Results and corrections that arrived while I worked changed three decisions (§7), and each was corrected.\n\n- Frank Odum (pt-0027), lisinopril 10 mg: NOT refilled. I first renewed it, because the outside K 5.9 from 8/27 was hemolyzed and the last valid K was 4.5 on 1/20. Then a new St. Brigid BMP from 10/20 arrived with an acceptable specimen and K 5.8. I cancelled the renewal (mr-t0001). The prior order mr-00283 is stopped. Urgent task task-t0011 to Dr. Okafor (focus mr-00283). The repeat BMP sr-t0002 is still open. Patient told, with ED precautions.\n- Samuel Price (pt-0030): 4 messages, two medications.\n  - Metformin 1000 mg BID: renewed for 90 days with 1 refill (mr-t0004). Corrected eGFR 58; outside HbA1c 7.1% from 8/19. The two pharmacy requests and the patient message were handled as one request.\n  - Lisinopril 20 mg: NOT refilled. Creatinine from 10/6 was corrected today from 1.36 to 1.49, which is 35.5% above the 1.10 before the 9/18 dose increase. I cancelled the renewal (mr-t0003). mr-00295 is stopped. Urgent task task-t0012 to Dr. Okafor (focus mr-00295). Patient told.\n- Marcus Webb (pt-0031):\n  - Metformin 500 mg BID: renewed for 90 days with 1 refill (mr-t0007). The 10/14 eGFR of 39 was entered in error and not used.\n  - Lisinopril 10 mg: at first there was no BMP in the last 12 months (last drawn 10/20/2025), so I sent a 30-day supply and ordered a BMP (sr-t0006). A valid BMP from 10/22 then arrived with K 4.6, so I replaced the 30-day order with a 90-day supply and 1 refill (mr-t0010). sr-t0006 is no longer needed and I have no tool to cancel it, so task task-t0019 asks Dr. Okafor to cancel it. Patient told.\n\nA protocol note is in each chart (doc-t0016, doc-t0017, doc-t0018). The three new-result items in the results queue (inbox-a0001, inbox-a0002, inbox-a0004) were reviewed and acted on above, but left open for Dr. Okafor. The other results-queue items were outside this request and were not touched.",
